comment.body:
This issue is pretty stale, mostly because I've forgotten about it. 

@raucao the current `/media` endpoints is intentionally limited to prevent this exact use case. blossom servers shouldn't become processing / transcoding servers since their primary role is to serve existing data. The existing `/media` endpoint was the simplest way I could think of to offload image optimization to a trusted server without the client needing to understand image optimization.

That said async and customizable media optimization is needed by lots of nostr clients. whether its HSL encoding or generating thumbnails someone needs to do the work but I don't think that should be blossom servers, I think it needs to be something else
